# `<p>x</q>` - nine bytes, and the only instrument in this tree that sees the
# defect in them is this one.
#
# html is the grammar the board calls genuinely clean: 72,288 bytes, 72,288
# built, 100.0% standing, zero damage, and `rack` scores viewer.html 13,971
# labeled brackets shared of 13,971 with zero askew and zero racked. That is a
# real result and it stays true. It is also bounded by what viewer.html holds.
#
# tree-sitter over viewer.html builds 13,972 nodes, 531 `element`s and 506
# `end_tag`s, and **zero** `erroneous_end_tag`. The corpus never presents a
# mismatched close, so no corpus instrument can have an opinion about one.
#
# `_erroneous_end_tag_name` is declared external precisely so a mismatched
# close is a named thing rather than damage. The oracle reads these nine bytes
# as ONE element:
#
#   element [0, 8)
#     start_tag [0, 3)
#     text [3, 4)
#     erroneous_end_tag [4, 8)
#       erroneous_end_tag_name [6, 7)
#
# joints produces three roots and no `element` at all - `start_tag`, `text`
# and `erroneous_end_tag` side by side, then `truncated; input ended before the
# start symbol closed`. Every leaf is identical to the oracle's, at identical
# extents, including the external this specimen was written for. Only the
# parent is missing.
#
# That is why four of these six claims hold. `holds erroneous_end_tag_name`,
# `spans erroneous_end_tag_name 6 7`, `spans text 3 4` and `mends 0` all pass:
# the lexing is right and nothing was repaired. `roots 1` and `holds element`
# fail, and they are the whole defect.
#
# `rack` cannot see it either, and this is worth stating plainly because rack
# is the most sensitive instrument here. Run against this specimen it reports
# 7 built, 7 square, 0 askew, 0 racked, 6 of 6 brackets shared - clean. It
# compares spines *inside built windows*, and a parent that was never built is
# in no window. Its `frames` column notices there are 2 frames where the oracle
# has 1, but `framed` only charges a frame whose NAME disagrees, so a parse
# that fragments into more frames than the oracle costs nothing. A wrong shape
# over right leaves was rack's founding example; a MISSING shape over right
# leaves is the same blind spot one step further out.
roots 1
mends 0
holds erroneous_end_tag_name
spans erroneous_end_tag_name 6 7
holds element
spans text 3 4
